vscode: three tabs, a find-and-replace on the log that you would have to undo twice
open: payment.service.ts capture.log errors.json

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    PAY-731  When the gateway times out on capture, we record the
             failure as PAYMENT_DECLINED. Customers are getting decline
             emails for orders that were never declined. Fix the
             service, and correct the excerpt attached to the incident
             so the write-up is accurate.

Three files, open as three buffers. `:w` before `:bn`, and `:wqa` to
finish — with three files open, `:wq` refuses.

  1. payment.service.ts — in `capture`, the branch for a `504` from the
     gateway throws `PAYMENT_DECLINED`. It should throw
     `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT`. The `402` branch is a real decline and
     keeps its code, and so does the fallback at the bottom.

  2. payment.service.ts — the retry predicate lists `502` and `503` as
     retryable statuses. Add `504` to that list, after `503`.

  3. capture.log — the excerpt attached to the incident. Every
     `payment.capture` line whose `gateway_status` is `504` records
     `reason=PAYMENT_DECLINED`; correct those to `reason=GATEWAY_TIMEOUT`.
     The lines with `gateway_status=402` are genuine declines and stay
     as they are.

  4. errors.json — nothing to add. `PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT` is already
     registered. It is open so you can check, and to be left alone.

@keys
| `/pattern` `Enter` then `2j` | search is still the fastest way to a line |
| `ci'` | change inside the quotes |
| `/503]/e` | land on the `]` — under `\v` the bracket would need its backslash |
| `i` | insert before the cursor |
| `504.*reason\=\zs` | context, a gap, more context, then the match starts |
| `cgn` then `.` | change the match, then the next |
| `:w` `:bn` `:wqa` | write, next buffer, write all and quit |

@hints
The service file has three `PAYMENT_DECLINED` strings. The one you want
is the one two lines under `504`. Search for the number, step down
twice, change inside the quotes.
--
For the retry list, land on the `]` after `503` and insert in front of
it. A search lands on the start of its match, so ask for the end with
`/e`. The bracket needs no escape in the default dialect.
--
In the log, the condition is `504` and the match is `PAYMENT_DECLINED`,
with a gap between them. `\zs` after the gap and the `reason=` puts the
cursor and the match on the reason alone, and `cgn` changes only that.
Three lines, so `cgn` once and `.` twice.
--
`:wqa` at the end. If `:wq` tells you there are more files to edit,
that is why.

@solution
**payment.service.ts** — `/504` `Enter`, `2j`, `ci'PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT`,
`Esc`. Then `/503]/e` `Enter`, `i, 504`, `Esc`. `:w`, `:bn`.

**capture.log** — `/504.*reason=\zsPAYMENT_DECLINED` `Enter` lands on
the reason of the first timed-out capture, and only those: the `402`
lines never match. `cgnGATEWAY_TIMEOUT`, `Esc`, `.`, `.`. `:wqa`.

**errors.json** — not touched.

About a hundred and fifteen keystrokes, sixty of them the two new codes.

The log is the part that this chapter was for. A plain search for
`PAYMENT_DECLINED` finds five lines, two of which must not change, and
you would be alternating `n` and `.` and checking the status on each
line by eye. The pattern carries the check — `504`, somewhere before
the reason — and `\zs` makes the match start where the edit starts, so
`cgn` and `.` do exactly three changes and no wrong ones. Context on
the left of `\zs`, edit on the right: that is the shape of most real
regex work in an editor, and it is a shape no other tool can express
without a replacement string.

The two edits in the service file used no regex at all. That is also
the lesson. A search for `504` and a `2j` is faster than any pattern
that could describe "the throw in the 504 branch", and the `503]`
search was plain text because the text was already unique — the only
trick was the `/e` offset, so that the cursor arrived on the bracket
rather than the number. Reach for a pattern when a literal lands on
the wrong thing first. When it does not, do not.

@start payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { GatewayClient } from './gateway.client';
import { logger } from '../logger';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(GatewayClient) protected gatewayClient: GatewayClient) {}

  public async capture(args: { orderId: string; amount: number; requestId: string }) {
    const response = await this.gatewayClient.post('/v2/payments', {
      orderId: args.orderId,
      amount: args.amount,
      idempotencyKey: args.requestId,
    });

    if (response.status === 201) {
      return response.data;
    }

    if (response.status === 402) {
      logger.warn('payment.capture declined', { orderId: args.orderId, requestId: args.requestId });
      throw exception('PAYMENT_DECLINED');
    }

    if (response.status === 504) {
      logger.warn('payment.capture timed out', { orderId: args.orderId, requestId: args.requestId });
      throw exception('PAYMENT_DECLINED');
    }

    const retryable = [502, 503].includes(response.status);

    if (retryable) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_GATEWAY_UNAVAILABLE');
    }

    throw exception('PAYMENT_DECLINED');
  }

  public async refund(orderId: string, amount: number) {
    const response = await this.gatewayClient.post('/v2/refunds', { orderId, amount });

    if (response.status !== 201) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { GatewayClient } from './gateway.client';
import { logger } from '../logger';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(GatewayClient) protected gatewayClient: GatewayClient) {}

  public async capture(args: { orderId: string; amount: number; requestId: string }) {
    const response = await this.gatewayClient.post('/v2/payments', {
      orderId: args.orderId,
      amount: args.amount,
      idempotencyKey: args.requestId,
    });

    if (response.status === 201) {
      return response.data;
    }

    if (response.status === 402) {
      logger.warn('payment.capture declined', { orderId: args.orderId, requestId: args.requestId });
      throw exception('PAYMENT_DECLINED');
    }

    if (response.status === 504) {
      logger.warn('payment.capture timed out', { orderId: args.orderId, requestId: args.requestId });
      throw exception('PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT');
    }

    const retryable = [502, 503, 504].includes(response.status);

    if (retryable) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_GATEWAY_UNAVAILABLE');
    }

    throw exception('PAYMENT_DECLINED');
  }

  public async refund(orderId: string, amount: number) {
    const response = await this.gatewayClient.post('/v2/refunds', { orderId, amount });

    if (response.status !== 201) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

